WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.440
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.110
And we see this beautiful picture here

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.980
of a mother with her baby.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.930
Here's the real story!

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.490
Don't forget we're telling this story

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.119
of the nun named Blue
Lotus or Indigo Lotus

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:20.077
because Pabongka Rinpoche

00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:22.880
wants to illustrate that,

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.710
as we go through life, things change,

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.620
our relationships change,

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:32.020
we never know what was going
on before or after this life.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.633
That's the theme behind this story.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.970
We went to The Sutra of
the Wise and the Foolish

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.140
and we found this story and
we're telling the whole story.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.140
Which is why this Lam Rim
is taking so many years.

00:00:46.259 --> 00:00:48.707
BDAG KYANG KUN TU RGYU
BA'I RIGS SU SKYES TE

00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:51.650
I was born into a KUN TU RGYU BA'I RIGS

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:56.010
This is a kind of a
religious Brahmin family

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.360
called Wanderers.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.420
They're not like Brahmins,

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.907
but they are a respectable,
religious Hindu family

00:01:02.907 --> 00:01:04.699
I was born into.

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:05.720
KHO MO'I.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.946
By the way, Tim, means me, as a woman.

00:01:08.946 --> 00:01:11.717
KHO MO'I PHA MA YANG RIGS CHE

00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:15.247
My parents were of a high caste and

00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:16.080
BTZUN PAS

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.329
they were also very religious.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:21.240
KHO MO YANG KUN TU RGYU RIGS CHE BA

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.240
They found for me

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.337
another person of the
same caste as a husband.

00:01:30.337 --> 00:01:31.170
MANG DU THOS PA

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.718
He was very learned.

00:01:32.718 --> 00:01:34.009
RIGS BYED DANG LDAN PA ZHEG

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:36.290
He knew the Vedas.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.685
He was a Veda master, which
is a very desirable husband.

00:01:40.685 --> 00:01:42.177
ZHEG LA BAG MAR BTANG

00:01:42.177 --> 00:01:45.181
They married me off to him

00:01:45.181 --> 00:01:47.097
NAS DE'I CHUNG MA BYED DE

00:01:47.097 --> 00:01:49.755
and I became his wife.

00:01:49.755 --> 00:01:53.430
CHUNG MA means little one, little lady

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:54.890
and it can mean wife,

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.750
but it can also mean younger wife

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.501
if the other person had two wives.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.587
DE'I BU YANG YOD PAR GYUR TO

00:02:02.587 --> 00:02:04.043
And we had a child together.

00:02:05.411 --> 00:02:10.377
PHYIS GYOS RGYUG TSE 'PHOS
PA'I 'OG TU KHO MO LA

00:02:10.377 --> 00:02:12.626
SEMS CAN YOD PAR GYUR

00:02:12.626 --> 00:02:15.876
Later on, my mother-in-law passed away,

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.730
and I became SEMS CAN YOD PA

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.030
For a hundred dollars, Tim.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.329
Oh I hope, you can probably
see it in the notes.

00:02:24.329 --> 00:02:26.410
SEMS CAN YOD PA

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:29.935
It took me about 10
minutes to figure it out.

00:02:31.859 --> 00:02:34.500
SEMS CAN YOD

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.778
Think of the context. She got married.

00:02:38.778 --> 00:02:41.100
- [Tim] (indistinct)

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.302
- Nah, forget it. She got pregnant.

00:02:43.302 --> 00:02:44.622
(laughter)
- [Tim] Oh, I see.

00:02:44.622 --> 00:02:47.687
- She got living-being-haver.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:52.339
It's cute. I finally said, Oh yeah, okay.

00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:53.237
SEMS CAN YOD PAR GYUR NAS

00:02:53.237 --> 00:02:55.125
She got pregnant and

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:56.097
KHYIM THAB

00:02:56.097 --> 00:03:00.796
she had servants in the
house, helpers in the house.

00:03:00.796 --> 00:03:03.630
LA, 'DI SKAD CES BYAS SO

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.060
And I said to the other servant,

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.214
to the servants in the house

00:03:07.214 --> 00:03:08.284
KHO MO LA SEMS CAN YOD

00:03:08.284 --> 00:03:10.191
I have a SEMS CAN

00:03:10.191 --> 00:03:12.073
I'm pregnant.

00:03:12.073 --> 00:03:13.289
ZLA BA YANG TSANG

00:03:13.289 --> 00:03:14.950
And the month are now full,

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.670
meaning nine months have passed,

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.271
or close to nine months.

00:03:18.271 --> 00:03:19.323
DU NYE BAS

00:03:19.323 --> 00:03:20.934
The time is near.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.970
GAL TE 'DIR BU BTZAS NA

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.924
If I give birth to my
child here in this house,

00:03:26.924 --> 00:03:27.757
BTZOG PO

00:03:27.757 --> 00:03:29.940
it's a little bit not so clean here and

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:30.773
MI BTUB

00:03:30.773 --> 00:03:34.252
it's not that convenient. So I'm thinking,

00:03:34.252 --> 00:03:37.751
KHO MO'I PHA MA'I KHYIM DU BTZAR 'GRO'O

00:03:37.751 --> 00:03:41.596
I'm going to go have my
child at my parents' home.

00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:43.516
KHO MO LA LEGS SO

00:03:43.516 --> 00:03:48.516
My house servants told
me that's a good idea.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:54.564
ZHES ZER TE, KHYO SHUG GNYIS 'GROGS NAS

00:03:54.564 --> 00:03:59.564
So two married couples of
servants accompanied me.

00:04:00.235 --> 00:04:03.580
BU ZHIG KYANG KHRID DE

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:06.484
I took a child with me and

00:04:06.484 --> 00:04:09.110
PHA MA 'DOD PAR SONG BA LAS

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.553
and I went to where my parents lived.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.994
I went to go to my parents.

00:04:16.994 --> 00:04:18.880
LAM PHYED TZAM DU PHYIN PA

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.281
Halfway to their house, along the road

00:04:22.281 --> 00:04:23.905
MNGAL MI BDE BAR GYUR

00:04:23.905 --> 00:04:27.294
I felt something uncomfortable in my womb.

00:04:27.294 --> 00:04:28.610
SHING ZHIG GI DRUNG DU

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.414
We stopped at the base of a tree.

00:04:31.414 --> 00:04:33.015
NAM PHYED TZAM NA

00:04:33.015 --> 00:04:35.286
Around midnight,

00:04:35.286 --> 00:04:36.399
BU BTZAS SO

00:04:36.399 --> 00:04:38.887
my child was born. My son was born.

00:04:40.151 --> 00:04:42.320
KHO MO'I KHYIM THAB KYANG LOGS SHIG

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.700
So now she has two boys with her

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.608
and the two couples.

00:04:47.608 --> 00:04:50.674
KHO MO'I KHYIM THAB KYANG
LOGS SHIG NA NYAL BA

00:04:50.674 --> 00:04:55.674
One of the couples set up camp nearby

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.996
where I was having my baby.

00:04:58.996 --> 00:05:01.130
MTSAN MO SBRUL GYIS ZIN TO

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:06.130
And they were attacked
by a snake in the night.

00:05:08.744 --> 00:05:12.437
MTSAN MO BOS NA CANG MI GRAG NAS

00:05:12.437 --> 00:05:15.803
They tried to call out
but no one heard them.

00:05:15.803 --> 00:05:17.150
NAM LANGS TE

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.265
And then the sun came up the next morning.

00:05:20.265 --> 00:05:21.098
BLTAS NA

00:05:21.098 --> 00:05:22.854
And I looked at their campsite.

00:05:22.854 --> 00:05:27.009
KHYIM THAB KYANG SBRUL
GDUG PAS ZIN PAS TSE 'PHOS

00:05:27.009 --> 00:05:30.130
I saw that the snake had killed them,

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.241
poisoned them with poison,

00:05:32.241 --> 00:05:33.850
LUS KYANG ZHIG PAR GYUR TO

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.890
and eaten their bodies mostly.

00:05:38.926 --> 00:05:41.157
DE'I TSE NA KHO MO 'KHAMS TE

00:05:41.157 --> 00:05:45.933
I passed out from the
shock and I fell down.

00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:48.641
SA LA 'GYEL BA

00:05:48.641 --> 00:05:51.414
And I ended up on the ground.

00:05:51.414 --> 00:05:55.190
BU CHE BA YANG PHA SBRUL GYIS BSAD PA

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:58.890
Then the older son,
that was already there,

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:03.343
his father died also, was
killed by another snake.

00:06:04.402 --> 00:06:08.710
MTHONG NAS SKAD PHYUNG STE NGUS PAS

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:11.943
I cried out in suffering and weeping.

00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:18.980
BU NGUS PA'I SKAD GYIS
KHO MO YANG PHYIR SANGS

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.510
Sorry, The boy started
crying and that woke me up.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.140
When he saw his father dead,

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.747
he was crying and that woke me up.

00:06:27.747 --> 00:06:30.050
And this larger child ...

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.380
So now I have two kids:

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.760
I have one previous son

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.170
who walked into the jungle with us

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:38.320
to go to my parents' house

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.390
so I could have the other child,

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.093
but the other child was
born suddenly at night.

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:45.873
So I put the older kid on my back.

00:06:46.932 --> 00:06:47.765
KHUR DU THOGS

00:06:47.765 --> 00:06:51.460
There's KHUR again, a load on the back.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.840
BU CHUNG BA NI

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.060
By the way, that sutra
was especially difficult

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.700
because in this one sentence,

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:02.540
there are one, two, three, four,

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:06.930
five, six spelling mistakes.

00:07:08.821 --> 00:07:11.417
THOGS BU CHUNG BA PHANG BAR KHYER TE

00:07:11.417 --> 00:07:15.180
I put the younger, the
new child, on my hip.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.371
And weeping as I went,

00:07:16.371 --> 00:07:18.040
SONG SONG SONG

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.922
I walked, and walked, and walked.

00:07:20.922 --> 00:07:23.320
LAM YANG DBEN PA ZHIG STE

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:27.720
Then I got to a

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.770
sort of a wild part of the forest,

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:32.521
desolate part of the forest.

00:07:32.521 --> 00:07:33.970
YANG MI 'DRUL

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:37.140
I couldn't find anyone to help me.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.630
There was no other person on the road

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:42.531
and it was passing to a deserted area.

00:07:42.531 --> 00:07:43.364
MA RNYED DO

00:07:43.364 --> 00:07:45.480
There's RNYED that we had

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:49.060
to find or to locate.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.620
BAR NA CHU CHEN PO

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.860
BAR NA here means there
came a time in the interim,

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.203
somewhere along the road,

00:07:57.203 --> 00:07:58.600
CHU CHEN PO ZHIG YOD DE

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.631
we came to a great river.

00:08:00.631 --> 00:08:03.489
CHU'I KHA TSO NA {%TSON}, misspelled.

00:08:03.489 --> 00:08:05.771
YANG CHE LA ZAB PAS

00:08:05.771 --> 00:08:08.911
The river was very wide and very deep.

00:08:08.911 --> 00:08:11.094
BU GNYI GA MA THEG NAS

00:08:11.094 --> 00:08:13.757
Here's THEG PA as 'yana',

00:08:13.757 --> 00:08:17.070
meaning, I didn't have
the vehicular capacity

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:19.100
to carry both kids.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:23.060
So there's a great ancient

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.460
use of the word THEG,

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.897
meaning to be able to carry.

00:08:28.727 --> 00:08:29.852
GNYI GA MA THEG

00:08:29.852 --> 00:08:32.517
I couldn't carry both
kids across the river. So,

00:08:32.517 --> 00:08:35.575
BU CHE BA NI CHU'I

00:08:35.575 --> 00:08:36.540
misspelled,

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.265
CHU {%TSU) ROL DU BZHAG

00:08:38.265 --> 00:08:40.223
extremely difficult misspelling.

00:08:40.223 --> 00:08:45.177
I left the one, the older
boy, on the near shore.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:51.331
And then I took the
younger boy, the newborn,

00:08:51.331 --> 00:08:52.740
BU CHUNG NGU KHYER TE

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.273
I carried him

00:08:54.273 --> 00:08:55.420
PHA ROL TU BSKYAL

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:59.433
and I forded across to the
other side of the river.

00:09:00.692 --> 00:09:04.807
BSKYAL NAS PHYIR CHE BA BSUR 'ONGS PA DANG

00:09:04.807 --> 00:09:06.441
And then I turned back.

00:09:06.441 --> 00:09:08.820
This PHYIR means turned back and the

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.157
CHE BA BSUR 'ONGS PA DANG means

00:09:10.157 --> 00:09:14.068
I went back to get the older boy

00:09:14.068 --> 00:09:18.360
on the near side, who I had left

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.970
while I would carry the
newborn to the other side.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:24.653
She sat the newborn on
the ground and came back.

00:09:25.757 --> 00:09:27.150
BU YANG MA 'ONG

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.480
And here it's confusing, because this MA

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.946
is not MA 'ONG, it's

00:09:30.946 --> 00:09:31.779
MA

00:09:31.779 --> 00:09:33.077
'ONG

00:09:33.077 --> 00:09:35.973
The older boy saw his mother coming.

00:09:37.261 --> 00:09:38.580
CHU'I NANG DU ZHUGS

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.861
So he stepped into the river.

00:09:41.861 --> 00:09:43.220
ZHUGS TE CHUS KHYER

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:47.020
and he was carried away by the current.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.950
KHO MOS BSNYAGS NA

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:50.684
And I reached out for him.

00:09:50.684 --> 00:09:53.201
STOBS CHUNG BSAM {%BAS MA} MA ZIN

00:09:53.201 --> 00:09:55.787
Misspelled.

00:09:55.787 --> 00:10:00.070
But I didn't have the
power to hold on to him.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.662
I got his arm, but I couldn't keep it on,

00:10:02.662 --> 00:10:04.670
I couldn't hold on to it.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.390
And the river carried him away.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:11.431
DE NAS PHYIR PHA ROL TU PHYIN

00:10:11.431 --> 00:10:13.281
Here's PHA ROL TU PHYIN PA in the

00:10:13.281 --> 00:10:15.797
ancient form to go to the other side.

00:10:15.797 --> 00:10:16.827
PHYIR means I went back.

00:10:16.827 --> 00:10:19.160
So I turned around and I went back

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.454
to the far side of the river.

00:10:21.454 --> 00:10:23.127
BU CHUNG NGU YANG

00:10:23.127 --> 00:10:28.015
SPYANG KIS means a coyote or a wolf.

00:10:29.398 --> 00:10:30.231
ZOS

00:10:30.231 --> 00:10:32.217
Past tense. Ate.

00:10:32.217 --> 00:10:35.380
And I realized the newborn had been eaten

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.936
by a wolf on the other side of the river.

00:10:38.936 --> 00:10:40.990
KHRAG CUNG ZAD TZAM SA LA SNANG NGO

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:45.990
And he was reduced to a
stain of blood in the soil,

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.600
a small puddle of blood in the soil.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.763
That's all that was left.

00:10:52.763 --> 00:10:54.487
DER YANG 'KHAMS NAS

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:55.607
Misspelled.

00:10:55.607 --> 00:10:59.953
I started to wander around in grief.

00:10:59.953 --> 00:11:02.400
RING ZHIG LON TE

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:06.767
After many, many hours and a few days

00:11:06.767 --> 00:11:07.600
SANGS PA

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.590
Here is the SANGS in SANGS RGYAS

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.990
which means to become aware.

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.620
So I came back to my senses.

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:18.076
These are ancient, ancient, useful words.

00:11:18.076 --> 00:11:20.719
SANGS PA DANG LAM DU ZHUGS TE

00:11:20.719 --> 00:11:24.052
I got back on the road
to my parents' house.

00:11:24.052 --> 00:11:26.350
SONG SONG SONG

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:28.643
I walked, and walked, and walked.

00:11:30.503 --> 00:11:32.853
KUN TU RGYU KHO MO'I PHA MA DANG NYE ZHING

00:11:32.853 --> 00:11:33.694
BSHES PA ZHIG

00:11:33.694 --> 00:11:38.280
Then I ran into a member
of the same caste,

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.090
who was a friend of my parents.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:42.790
The Wandering caste.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:47.773
PHRAD NAS KUN TU RGYU DES KHYOD CI NYES NA

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:50.874
'DI LTAR NYON MONGS PAR GYUR CES DRIS NA

00:11:50.874 --> 00:11:52.465
What's wrong with you?

00:11:52.465 --> 00:11:55.030
And why have you gotten
so NYON MONGS PAed?

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.720
What's distressing you?

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:59.697
There's the ancient meaning of NYON MONGS.

00:11:59.697 --> 00:12:02.030
What's distressing you so badly?

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.838
KHO MOS KYANG JI LTAR GYUR
PA RGYAS PAR GTAM BYAS

00:12:05.838 --> 00:12:09.758
So I told him the whole story extensively.

00:12:09.758 --> 00:12:12.694
GTAM means to tell a story,

00:12:12.694 --> 00:12:14.342
told him the whole story.

00:12:14.342 --> 00:12:17.550
KUN TU RGYU DE YANG DUS (%NGUS)

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:18.387
Misspelled.

00:12:18.387 --> 00:12:22.028
He started to weep also and

00:12:22.028 --> 00:12:24.028
KHO MOS PHA MA'I GTAM DRIS NA

00:12:24.028 --> 00:12:26.440
And then I said, 'How
are my parents doing?'

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:28.190
And he said,

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:33.190
'KHYOD KYI PHA MA'I KHYM DU DE BAR ME SHOR

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:36.130
Your parents' house caught on fire

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.840
since the last time you heard from them.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.413
PHA MA DANG KHYIM GANG GI MI THAMS CAD

00:12:41.413 --> 00:12:43.560
Your mother, your father, and everybody

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.973
in the house was burned to death.

00:12:45.973 --> 00:12:50.556
MES TSIG GO, ZHES ZER RO

00:12:51.847 --> 00:12:53.776
He told me.

00:12:53.776 --> 00:12:55.977
DE SKAD CES SMRAS PA
THOS NAS KHO MO 'KHAMS TE

00:12:55.977 --> 00:12:58.740
When I heard what happened to my parents,

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:02.560
I passed out again and fell to the earth.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:03.460
